{"uid":"dfaa58776846caf9","name":"test_script_injects_nothing_when_no_usable_docker_socket_is_present","fullName":"tests.test_host_like_pytest_script#test_script_injects_nothing_when_no_usable_docker_socket_is_present","historyId":"48ef757220e5281d59032a47c1d65a0b","time":{"start":1791925248271,"stop":1791925251143,"duration":2872},"description":"Pins the socket-absent direction (#109). Chosen policy: **injects\n    nothing, docker-marked tests self-skip at runtime** -- when this\n    script's own probe finds no usable docker socket (mirroring a bare\n    developer host), it must NOT add ``-m \"not docker\"`` on the caller's\n    behalf. The docker-marked module is left to its own module-level\n    ``skipif`` (``tests/test_docker_sibling_e2e.py``'s\n    ``_docker_available()``) to self-skip cleanly at runtime, the same way\n    it would for a developer invoking the bare acceptance command by hand\n    with no socket around. Proven here at collection time: with\n    ``DOCKER_SOCK_PATH`` pointed at a path that does not exist (so the\n    script's own ``-S`` probe fails regardless of any ambient docker socket\n    this container happens to have), the docker-marked module's tests are\n    still *collected* (no ``-m \"not docker\"`` deselection), unlike the\n    usable-socket case above where they are deselected to zero.","descriptionHtml":"<p>Pins the socket-absent direction (#109). Chosen policy: <strong>injects<br />\nnothing, docker-marked tests self-skip at runtime</strong> -- when this<br />\nscript's own probe finds no usable docker socket (mirroring a bare<br />\ndeveloper host), it must NOT add <code>-m &quot;not docker&quot;</code> on the caller's<br />\nbehalf. The docker-marked module is left to its own module-level<br />\n<code>skipif</code> (<code>tests/test_docker_sibling_e2e.py</code>'s<br />\n<code>_docker_available()</code>) to self-skip cleanly at runtime, the same way<br />\nit would for a developer invoking the bare acceptance command by hand<br />\nwith no socket around. Proven here at collection time: with<br />\n<code>DOCKER_SOCK_PATH</code> pointed at a path that does not exist (so the<br />\nscript's own <code>-S</code> probe fails regardless of any ambient docker socket<br />\nthis container happens to have), the docker-marked module's tests are<br />\nstill <em>collected</em> (no <code>-m &quot;not docker&quot;</code> deselection), unlike the<br />\nusable-socket case above where they are deselected to zero.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791925216356,"stop":1791925216356,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791925216356,"stop":1791925216357,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1791925248249,"stop":1791925248249,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"start":1791925248250,"stop":1791925248260,"duration":10},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_task_record_dir","time":{"start":1791925248260,"stop":1791925248260,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_scrub_notifier_env_in_